# The organisers' handbook is their material, not mine to redistribute.
source/antibody-design-hackathon-handbook.*

# Syncthing conflict copies -- vault sync artefacts, never part of the repo.
*.sync-conflict-*

# data/refs/*.pdb above does NOT recurse into prepared/, which is the only reason the
# DockQ reference ships at all. That was luck, not design. Keep it deliberate: the
# validator defaults to data/refs/prepared/5ggs_ABZ.pdb and a clone without it cannot
# reproduce the Challenge 1 DockQ. Do not add data/refs/**/*.pdb.
!data/refs/prepared/5ggs_ABZ.pdb

# A private strategic assessment of named, identifiable third parties: it is tagged
# job-search, names a private WhatsApp channel, identifies a co-founder, and speculates
# about an employer' unpublished commercial thesis. Fine as personal notes; not something
# to attach permanently to a public repo under my own name. Kept locally, not published.
knowledge/Locksmith Bio — Company Context.md

# --- RFdiffusion / Hydra run artefacts (added 2026-09-28) -------------------
# The decoy control runs with cwd = repo root, so Hydra writes run logs to
# outputs/ and RFdiffusion caches its noise schedules beside them. A `git add -A`
# during a live run swept a 7.8 MB generated .pkl and 12 Hydra logs into three
# commits. Generated caches are not source; they are also the kind of file a
# reader of a published repo has to stop and wonder about.
outputs/
cached_schedules/
T_*_omega_*_schedule_*.pkl
